MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The adjustable power supply would help me power and test circuits built with my breadboards, relay module, and PCB components, making it a practical next purchase.",
    "The oscilloscope fits the same hands-on electronics work because it would help me inspect signals and troubleshoot circuits, although its measurement limits matter."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The printer and filament assume a printing project or printer ownership that my purchases do not establish; building electronic circuits does not give me an immediate need for printing supplies.",
    "The thermal camera has a plausible troubleshooting use, but I have no specific task requiring it beyond my infrared thermometer. The tap kit and spring hook also need particular jobs that I have not shown, while the soap dispenser has no clear connection to my current projects."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in electronics seems to have been stretched into a broad interest in anything associated with DIY projects, especially 3D printing.",
    "An occasional mechanical purchase seems to have been treated as interest in specialized workshop tools, even when there is no evidence I need their particular function."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My breadboards, battery holder, relay, and PCB supplies point toward assembling, powering, and testing small circuits; recommendations that directly support those tasks matter most to me.",
    "I choose equipment when it solves a concrete project need. A possible future use is not enough, especially when an item requires other equipment or overlaps with a tool I already have."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my circuit-building interests but extended them too broadly into printing supplies and specialized tools without a clear current use."
}
